diff --git a/roadmap/performance.md b/roadmap/performance.md
index 95f6133..0e9140d 100644
--- a/roadmap/performance.md
+++ b/roadmap/performance.md
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ Not applicable, left out on purpose: multi-draw and persistent mapping (not in w
 - 2026-10-21 (9): dynamic resolution (the step 4 above; GPUBooster / Sodium have no counterpart, idea of console dynamic-res) (written with a Rust toolchain for the controller only: `gpu::context::drs_tests::steps_down_when_gpu_bound_and_probes_up_with_backoff` ran and passed standalone under rustc 1.73; the crate was NOT compiled and not run on a device; run `cargo test --lib --release context options` first):
     - `RENDER_SCALE` (0.67 = `START_PCT`) is only where the scene scale starts. `gpu::context::Drs` moves it by 5 points between 50% and 100% from the time `render_frame` takes (swap-chain wait included) and the CPU part of it (the same `acq` split as the FPS line): a window of 30 frames averaging 20% over 60 Hz while the CPU is under 75% of it is GPU-bound, so it steps down; a slow window with a busy CPU changes nothing and does not count as clean. vsync hides spare GPU time, so it probes up after 20 clean windows (10 s at 60 fps); a drop within 3 windows of a probe doubles the wait (max 240), a probe that holds halves it.
     - Plumbing, nothing duplicated: `scene_size` reads the static scale; `Gpu::rescale` is the depth half of `Gpu::resize` (no `surface.configure`); `App::sync_scene` is the `Present::resize` half of `App::resize`. A step recreates the depth, the MSAA colour, the 1-sample scene and the final pass's bind group, once, at the end of the frame after `present()`; FXAA/CAS are untouched (CAS taps follow the scene size from `Present`'s uniform).
-    - Kill switch: `dynamicRes:false` in `options.txt` (no button, like `gpuErrorTrace`) pins the scale at `START_PCT`. The log prints `dynamic resolution: scene at N%` at every step.
+    - Kill switch: the `Dynamic Res: ON/OFF` button in Video Settings (2026-10-22 (3); `dynamicRes:` in `options.txt`) pins the scale at `START_PCT` at once when it goes off. The log prints `dynamic resolution: scene at N%` at every step.
     - ponytail: a fixed 60 Hz target (on a 90 / 120 Hz panel it only fires below 60 fps); no GPU timestamps (wgpu `TIMESTAMP_QUERY` is not on every GLES fallback), so a GPU-bound frame is inferred from the swap-chain wait. UNVERIFIED on a device: that `Present::resize` every few seconds does not hitch (a Mali tiler reallocating the MSAA target), whether 100% is ever reached with MSAA 4x, and `SCALE_MAX` (lower it to 85 if the probes overshoot).
 - 2026-10-21 (8): frame passes 3 -> 2, MSAA 4x instead of FXAA, face shade baked into the chunk vertex; compressed atlas MEASURED, NOT wired (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; new tests `present::tests::{the_present_chain_is_one_pass, coverage_needs_samples}`, `pipeline::tests::chunk_layers_have_no_derivative_shade`, `chunks::tests::flat_quads_carry_their_face_shade`; `present_shader_validates`, `chunk_shader_validates`, `frame_renders_headless` and `packed_quads_draw_the_mesher_triangles` (expectation changed: a flat quad now carries its face shade) must pass; run `cargo test --lib --release present pipeline chunks` first). From a review of where a phone GPU pays: bandwidth of full-screen passes, then texture reads.
     - **1. Fewer full-screen passes** (`render/present.rs`). Pass A (FXAA + CAS into the `ldr` texture, scene size) and pass B (upscale + vignette + HUD) are one pass now: `fs_fin` runs at surface size, reads the scene with taps one SCENE texel apart (so CAS still sharpens exactly what the upscale softens) and writes the swap chain. The `ldr` target (4 bytes a scene pixel, written then read) is gone. Cost to know: with FXAA in (no MSAA) its taps run at surface size, 2.2x the pixels of the old pass A at `RENDER_SCALE` 0.67; the edge branch is rare, the 5 taps are not. A render scale of 1.0 would make the pass pair a plain copy anyway: with MSAA the FXAA branch is compiled out (`@FXAA@`).
